181
00:11:24,410 --> 00:11:26,630
regarding the tattoo on his left chest.

182
00:11:27,120 --> 00:11:28,120
This tattoo

183
00:11:28,160 --> 00:11:29,500
is called a "Weretiger."

184
00:11:29,690 --> 00:11:31,520
It's a Lanna belief

185
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:33,670
about those who possess sacred arts and,

186
00:11:33,690 --> 00:11:34,630
as they grow old,

187
00:11:34,650 --> 00:11:36,820
can no longer control them.

188
00:11:36,970 --> 00:11:38,760
They eventually shapeshift into tigers.

189
00:11:39,220 --> 00:11:40,790
It's similar to "Saming Tigers," Lieutenant.

190
00:11:41,390 --> 00:11:42,430
"Saming tigers" are...

191
00:11:42,450 --> 00:11:43,650
tigers that eat humans

192
00:11:44,020 --> 00:11:45,020
and become possessed by their spirits,

193
00:11:45,420 --> 00:11:46,670
thus able to shapeshift into humans.

194
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:49,090
As for the Weretigers Inspector Chon said,

195
00:11:49,410 --> 00:11:50,920
they're humans
able to shapeshift into tigers.

196
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:58,100
And how is that
relevant to Krating, Inspector?

197
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:00,820
It's relevant because this Weretiger group

198
00:12:00,990 --> 00:12:03,760
holds sway across the borders of

199
00:12:03,780 --> 00:12:04,890
